zh.prompt:
以下是一場會議的筆記：

{notes}

會議標題：{title}
日期：{date}，長度：{duration}
與會者：{participants}

根據這些筆記，寫一封寄給全體與會者的電子郵件內文（不要寫主旨）：先問候，再用一段話說明會議重點，接著分別列出決議事項、待辦事項與負責人、尚未解決的問題，最後提醒內容由 AI 依錄音自動整理，請以錄音為準。只寫筆記裡有的內容，不要加入筆記沒有的人名、日期或承諾；提到某件事時在句尾附上筆記的時間，例如 [1:23]。

en.prompt:
Here are the notes of a meeting:

{notes}

Title: {title}
Date: {date}, length: {duration}
Participants: {participants}

From these notes, write the body of an e-mail in English to all the participants (no subject line): a greeting, one paragraph on the main points, then the decisions, the action items with their owners, and the open issues, and end by saying that the notes were generated by AI from the recording and should be checked against it. Only write what is in the notes; do not add names, dates or commitments that are not in them; when you mention something, end the sentence with the note's time, e.g. [1:23].

zh.prompt:
以下是一場會議的筆記：

{notes}

根據這些筆記，寫兩到四句話，告訴與會者這場會議最重要的結果：決定了什麼、誰要做什麼、還有什麼沒解決。不要問候、不要條列、不要標題。只寫筆記裡有的內容；每句句尾附上筆記的時間，例如 [1:23]。

en.prompt:
Here are the notes of a meeting:

{notes}

From these notes, write two to four sentences in English telling the participants the most important outcomes of this meeting: what was decided, who will do what, and what is still open. No greeting, no bullet points, no headings. Only write what is in the notes; end each sentence with the note's time, e.g. [1:23].

zh.prompt:
以下是一場會議的筆記：

{notes}

根據這些筆記，用連貫的段落寫一份會議摘要（不要條列、不要標題），說明討論了什麼、決定了什麼、誰要做什麼、還有什麼沒解決。只寫筆記裡有的內容；提到某件事時在句尾附上筆記的時間，例如 [1:23]。

en.prompt:
Here are the notes of a meeting:

{notes}

From these notes, write a summary of the meeting in English as connected paragraphs (no bullet points, no headings): what was discussed, what was decided, who will do what, and what is still open. Only write what is in the notes; when you mention something, end the sentence with the note's time, e.g. [1:23].

zh.prompt:
以下是一場會議的筆記，每則筆記括號裡是它的類型（DECISION 決議、ACTION 待辦、PROPOSAL 提議、OPEN-ISSUE 未決、NUMBER 數字）：

{notes}

根據這些筆記，寫兩到四句話，告訴與會者這場會議最重要的結果。只有 DECISION 筆記可以寫成「決定」；PROPOSAL 只能寫成「有人提議」或「建議」；OPEN-ISSUE 要寫成尚未解決；沒有 DECISION 筆記時，就寫「這次會議沒有做出明確決議」。不要問候、不要條列、不要標題。只寫筆記裡有的內容；每句句尾附上筆記的時間，例如 [1:23]。

en.prompt:
Here are the notes of a meeting; the word in brackets is each note's type (DECISION, ACTION, PROPOSAL, OPEN-ISSUE, NUMBER):

{notes}

From these notes, write two to four sentences in English telling the participants the most important outcomes of this meeting. Only a DECISION note may be called decided or agreed; a PROPOSAL must be written as a suggestion or proposal; an OPEN-ISSUE as still open; if there is no DECISION note, say that no firm decision was made. No greeting, no bullet points, no headings. Only write what is in the notes; end each sentence with the note's time, e.g. [1:23].
